name 'thinking-critically-about-ai-postassessment-q11_2026-pilot'

question 'A student argues: "Using AI to generate images for my project is fine because the AI just combines existing images — it isn\'t really creating anything new." Which response best challenges this reasoning?'

wrong 'The student is correct. AI image generators only copy and paste from existing images, so there are no concerns.'
wrong 'The student is wrong because AI tools are never allowed to be used for school projects.'
wrong 'The student is correct, but they still need to cite the specific images the AI used as sources.'
right 'The student\'s reasoning oversimplifies how AI works and ignores concerns about intellectual property, the environmental cost of running generative AI, and the importance of human creative contribution.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

